  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study to operationalize the Gender Resource Allocation and Result Tracking System (GRARTS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The innovative study seeks to institutionalize a gender perspective into the bank&#x2019;s operational documents.  The project experienced initial start-up delays but is now operational.  Currently, the Bank is exploring how to adopt the OECD / DAC Gender Equality Policy Marker, which is used by bilateral and multilateral development agencies to develop and institutionalize quality standards for gender mainstreaming. The expected developmental outcome is to make positive changes in the lives of women, men, girls and boys in Africa.
Approved: CAD 62,085 (disbursed or 63%)</narrative>
  </description>
